Taco Labs is the name I put on quick AI product bets. The main code sprint was summer 2025. Level Up Your Kid was a gamified parenting app, pitched as Duolingo for parenting. LoveStory generated personalized, illustrated love-story books. ARMA was a DeFi research agent. Smaller mocks sat around those: an AI health coach, a website-testing bot driven by personas, and a computer-vision test bench.

Most of it never left the mock stage. What's worth showing is how the mocks were built: a written set of rules for faking an app convincingly, and one manifest file that generated every image in it.

The label has its own brand too: a cream background, an orange primary and a green accent, a taco mark in solid and regular weights, and pill and square buttons with hover states.

